#heading(level: 2, numbering: none, outlined: false)[Set Theory]

$emptyset =$ empty set

$abs(A) = op("card") A =$ number of elements in set $A$

#source(18)
$A subset.eq B$ set inclusion

$A subset B$ proper inclusion of sets

$F compose G$ composition of maps (first $G$, then $F$)

$forall x$ for all $x$

$arrow.r.double$ implies

$arrow.l.r.double$ if and only if

$dot(union)$ disjoint union

#heading(level: 2, numbering: none, outlined: false)[Miscellaneous]

$bb(Z) =$ ring of rational integers

$bb(Q) =$ rational field

$bb(R) =$ real field

$bb(C) =$ complex field

$a divides b$ $a$ divides $b$ (for elements or ideals)

$a divides.not b$ $a$ does not divide $b$ (for elements or ideals)

$p^m parallel a$ means $p^m divides a$, $p^(m+1) divides.not a$

#heading(level: 2, numbering: none, outlined: false)[Group Theory]

$H <= G$ ($H < G$) subgroup inclusion (proper inclusion)

$H ⊴ G$ ($H ⊲ G$) $H$ is a normal subgroup of $G$ (proper)

$abs(G) = op("card") G$, $abs(G colon H) =$ index of $H$ in $G$

$⟨ x ⟩ =$ cyclic group generated by $x$

$⟨ x, y, dots ⟩ =$ group generated by the elements $x, y, dots$

$G_1 times G_2 =$ direct product of groups

$H ⋊ K =$ semidirect product of normal subgroup $H$ with subgroup $K$

$G slash H = {x H: x in G} =$ left cosets of $H$ in $G$

$H without G = {H x: x in G} =$ right cosets of $H$ in $G$

$H without G slash K = {H x K: x in G} =$ collection of $(H,K)$-double cosets in
$G$

$C_G lr(( )) =$ centralizer in $G$; $N_G lr(( )) =$ normalizer in $G$

$attach(=, br: G)$, $(attach(<=, br: G))$ equality (or inclusion) up to
$G$-conjugacy

#heading(level: 2, numbering: none, outlined: false)[Linear Algebra]

$op("Tr")(x,M) =$ trace of $x$ acting on $M$

$M_n lr((R)) =$ ring of $n times n$ matrices over a ring $R$

$R^(m times n) =$ additive group of $m times n$ matrices over $R$

$op("GL")_n lr((R)) =$ group of invertible $n times n$ matrices over $R$

$op("SL")_n lr((R)) = {X in op("GL")_n lr((R)): op("det") X = 1}$, if $R$ is
commutative

$attach(upright(bold(X)), tl: t) =$ transpose of matrix $upright(bold(X))$

#source(19)
$op("Tr") upright(bold(X)) =$ trace of matrix $upright(bold(X))$

$op("char. pol.") upright(bold(X)) =$ characteristic polynomial of matrix
$upright(bold(X))$

$op("diag")(a_1,dots,a_n) =$ diagonal matrix with diagonal entries
$a_1,dots,a_n$

#heading(level: 2, numbering: none, outlined: false)[Rings and Modules]

$R G =$ group algebra of a finite group $G$ over a commutative ring $R$

$op("Hom")_A lr((M,N)) =$ group of homomorphisms from $A$-module $M$ to
$A$-module $N$

$op("End")_A M = op("Hom")_A lr((M,M))$

$op("id")_M$, $1_M =$ identity map on module $M$

$limits(∐)_(i in I) M_i$, $M_1 ∔ M_2$, $M_1 ∐ M_2 =$ external direct sums of
modules

$limits(⊕)_(i in I) M_i$, $M_1 ⊕ M_2 =$ internal direct sums of modules

$M^((s)) =$ direct sum of $s$ copies of $M$

$op("ann")_A M = {a in A: a M = 0} =$ annihilator of $M$

$mu_A lr((M)) =$ minimal number of generators of $M$ as $A$-module

$x_r =$ right multiplication by $x$; $x_l =$ left multiplication by $x$

$c(A) =$ center of ring $A$

$attach(A, bl: A) =$ left regular module ($=$ ring $A$, as left $A$-module)

$u(A) = A^dot =$ units of ring $A$

$A^"o" =$ opposite ring of $A$

#heading(level: 2, numbering: none, outlined: false)[Category Theory]

$frak(A B) =$ category of abelian groups

$attach(frak(M), bl: A) =$ category of left $A$-modules ($A =$ ring)

$attach(frak(M), bl: A, br: B) =$ category of $A,B$-bimodules

$attach(op("mod"), bl: A) =$ category of f.g. left $A$-modules

$cal(P)(A) =$ category of f.g. projective left $A$-modules

#heading(level: 2, numbering: none, outlined: false)[Representation Theory]

$M hash N =$ outer tensor product of modules

$op("Irr")(G) =$ full set of irreducible complex characters of group $G$

$op("Irr")_K lr((G)) =$ full set of characters afforded by simple $K G$-modules

$op("Ind") R G =$ set of indecomposable $R G$-lattices

$op("ch") K G =$ ring of virtual characters afforded by $K G$-modules

$op("Bch") k G =$ ring of Brauer characters of $G$

$op("cf")_K lr((G)) =$ ring of $K$-valued class functions on $G$
